# Polopine UI

Vite + React + TypeScript polling app. Sibling repo `polopine-backend` is an Express API on Render.
Both repos may be cloned together in the `polopine` multi-repo Cloud Agent environment.

## Run commands

```bash
npm install         # idempotent
npm test            # vitest + Testing Library + jsdom
npm run typecheck   # tsc --noEmit
npm run dev         # vite on port 3000
npm run build       # tsc --noEmit && vite build
```

Green run before opening any PR: `npm install && npm run typecheck && npm test`.

## Conventions

- No shared imports with `polopine-backend`. Types are duplicated on purpose.
- Read backend origin from `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` (default `http://localhost:8080`).
- Public origin for the QR code comes from `VITE_PUBLIC_URL`, falling back to `window.location.origin`.
- `localStorage` is the source of truth for "have I voted on this poll?" markers.
- Plain CSS only — no UI frameworks. Match the existing visual language.
- Cover new components / pages with vitest + Testing Library tests.

## Cloud Agent specifics

- Secrets you may need from Cursor Settings → Cloud Agents → Secrets:
  - `VITE_API_URL` — backend base URL (no trailing slash)
  - `VITE_PUBLIC_URL` — Vercel production URL, used by the join QR code
- A `beforeShellExecution` hook blocks `rm -rf`, `git push --force[-with-lease]`, and `git reset --hard`.
  If a command is denied, pick a safer alternative — do not try to bypass it.
- When part of multi-repo, the backend repo is checked out as a sibling. Read it
  to keep request/response shapes in sync, but only open PRs in the repo a change
  actually belongs to.

## Out of scope (don't touch unless asked)

- UI framework / component library
- Replacing React Router
- Cross-repo imports from `polopine-backend`
